},{"type":"text","text":" patch, which wires its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"output "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card snaps back to its resting position."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/onKeyPress(_:action:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/onKeyPress(_:action:)","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"onKeyPress(_:action:)","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/onkeypress(_:action:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"onKeyPress","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"KeyEquivalent","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI13KeyEquivalentV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"action","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KeyPress","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI8KeyPressV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI8KeyPressV6ResultO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"View","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"title":"Swami","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami"}}}